# Controls what `agents-cli deploy` packages into the Agent Runtime container.
# This file REPLACES .gitignore for deploy-time file selection, so every
# .gitignore pattern that matters must be repeated here.

# --- Private strategy layer — MUST NEVER be packaged -----------------------
# These are symlinks into the private keplaria-strategy repo. Beyond the
# confidentiality rule, the packager resolves symlinks and aborts with
# "path is outside the project directory" if they are included.
strategy
.claude
CLAUDE.md

# --- Secrets ---------------------------------------------------------------
.env

# --- Python-generated ------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/
*.egg-info
.venv

# --- Not needed at runtime -------------------------------------------------
.git
.gitignore
.codex
.agents
deployment/
infra/
spikes/
scripts/
tests/
docs/
GEMINI.md
agents-cli-manifest.yaml
skills-lock.json
.rumdl_cache

# NOTE: `policy/` is deliberately NOT listed above and must NEVER be added to
# this "not needed at runtime" block. app/risk.py's DEFAULT_POLICY_PATH
# resolves to policy/supplier_risk.v1.json at runtime — it is the first
# runtime-required file outside app/. If this directory is ever excluded
# here, load_policy() fails on every case (fail-closed by design), which
# means every case silently becomes POLICY_UNAVAILABLE -> blocked: a total,
# silent onboarding outage that no test in this repo would catch, because
# tests run against the checked-out tree, not the deployed container.

# --- Local scratch: worktrees and SDD workspaces ---------------------------
# .gcloudignore REPLACES .gitignore at deploy time, so these must be repeated
# here. A worktree under .worktrees/ carries its own resolved strategy/.claude/
# CLAUDE.md symlinks — packaging one would leak the private layer (or abort the
# packager with "path is outside the project directory").
.worktrees/
.superpowers/
.playwright-mcp/
